# Example project note — DELETE or replace me

A format example. A real note is short and specific: the standing rule you'd otherwise repeat every time you touch this area of *this* project.

Trigger (add to `.claude/project-notes/INDEX.md`):
`| Background jobs, the nightly import | .claude/project-notes/jobs.md |`

Example content:

- The nightly import runs **in-process**, not via the external cron endpoint — this deployment is always-on, so `background-jobs.md`'s scale-to-zero wakeup path doesn't apply here. (Deviation from a workflow preference, confirmed 2026-07-24.)
- Imports are idempotent by `(source_id, day)` — a re-run must never double-insert.
- Never log the raw supplier payload; it contains customer names.

Note the shape of the first line: when a note overrides a workflow preference, **name the preference and why**, so the next reader sees a decision rather than a contradiction.

Replace this file with your own notes, and delete the example once you have real ones.
